(2531481, 347943, 51538, '<td valign="top">I''ve been back and forth to this photo a few times and cannot find immediate words to add.  What comes to mind is solitary.  I''d be interested to see this in b/w gradient applied or duotone of a more sepia type nature.  That, IMO, would enhance the desolate part of the symbolism you have tried to present.  I look at the photo as it stands and places like Lake Chad or Namibia come to mind for some odd reason.</td>', 'I''ve been back and forth to this photo a few times and cannot find immediate words to add.  What comes to mind is solitary.  I''d be interested to see this in b/w gradient applied or duotone of a more sepia type nature.  That, IMO, would enhance the desolate part of the symbolism you have tried to present.  I look at the photo as it stands and places like Lake Chad or Namibia come to mind for some odd reason.', '2006-06-20 10:20:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2531483, 347784, 51538, '<td valign="top">Looks like a nice location.  Green is rather hard, IMO, to make desolate.  Green as a visual symbol implies verdent, fertile, all things bright and beautiful, if you know what I mean.  Red rich soil tends to say something similar.  I wonder if you had composed the image more through the broken old tunnel or bridge if there was a more desolate viewpoint which you could then have enhanced by reducing the saturation of the colours.</td>', 'Looks like a nice location.  Green is rather hard, IMO, to make desolate.  Green as a visual symbol implies verdent, fertile, all things bright and beautiful, if you know what I mean.  Red rich soil tends to say something similar.  I wonder if you had composed the image more through the broken old tunnel or bridge if there was a more desolate viewpoint which you could then have enhanced by reducing the saturation of the colours.', '2006-06-20 10:22:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2531488, 349002, 51538, '<td valign="top">Those bricks surely tell a story of erosion.  They''re beyind repointing!  They must be subject to some extremes to have worn like that.</td>', 'Those bricks surely tell a story of erosion.  They''re beyind repointing!  They must be subject to some extremes to have worn like that.', '2006-06-20 10:23:46.000000', NULL, 1),
