(2555491, 349299, 40718, '<td valign="top">I think the picture is a good one.  Fits the subject well.  A few small issues:<br/> <br/>1) USM, if you used it, left a halo around the smokestacks.  You could use the history brush to get rid of that.<br/>2) Tilted horizon?  Could be an optical effect.  I would have levelled the roofline in the building and let the other lines fall where they may.<br/>3) You are a bit of a victim from the small canvas size.  There just isn''t a ton of detail in the garbage.  Some pictures suffer more than others from the 640 pixels.<br/></td>', 'I think the picture is a good one.  Fits the subject well.  A few small issues: 1) USM, if you used it, left a halo around the smokestacks.  You could use the history brush to get rid of that.2) Tilted horizon?  Could be an optical effect.  I would have levelled the roofline in the building and let the other lines fall where they may.3) You are a bit of a victim from the small canvas size.  There just isn''t a ton of detail in the garbage.  Some pictures suffer more than others from the 640 pixels.', '2006-06-26 17:11:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2555504, 348991, 40718, '<td valign="top">Desolation was a tricky challenge.  First 5.3 isn''t bad at all, but to get the higher score you needed to carry that desolate feel AND have a subject of emphasis.  Certainly this is as desolate as any shot...but it doesn''t have something to grab our eye.  In fact, the moon does that the most, which pulls us away from the desolate mountainside.<br/> <br/>Look at the Top 10 shots and notice how they capture the same feel, but still have a subject.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-26 16:17:48.</i></td>', 'Desolation was a tricky challenge.  First 5.3 isn''t bad at all, but to get the higher score you needed to carry that desolate feel AND have a subject of emphasis.  Certainly this is as desolate as any shot...but it doesn''t have something to grab our eye.  In fact, the moon does that the most, which pulls us away from the desolate mountainside. Look at the Top 10 shots and notice how they capture the same feel, but still have a subject.', '2006-06-26 17:16:02.000000', '2006-06-26 17:17:48.000000', 0),
(2555505, 349461, 50231, '<td valign="top">Awesome Shermy just awesome! The colors and post are great and I love the composition and idea. This should have won a ribbon.<br/> <br/>Erick<br/> <br/>:-)</td>', 'Awesome Shermy just awesome! The colors and post are great and I love the composition and idea. This should have won a ribbon. Erick :-)', '2006-06-26 17:16:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2555606, 349307, 40718, '<td valign="top">Composition, focus and PP are nicely done.  The lighting is really tough and it would have been nearly impossible not to have areas of blown highlight outside the path.<br/> <br/>I could quickly tell this would be at the top of my 4.5-5.5 scale.  I think the biggest issue simple pertains to what enough people considered "desolate".  Perhaps the "nice warmth" you added with the duotone worked against you in this regard.  I don''t think it was a biggie though, but I''m not looking for "nice" in desolate...</td>', 'Composition, focus and PP are nicely done.  The lighting is really tough and it would have been nearly impossible not to have areas of blown highlight outside the path. I could quickly tell this would be at the top of my 4.5-5.5 scale.  I think the biggest issue simple pertains to what enough people considered "desolate".  Perhaps the "nice warmth" you added with the duotone worked against you in this regard.  I don''t think it was a biggie though, but I''m not looking for "nice" in desolate...', '2006-06-26 17:59:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2555616, 348416, 39184, '<td valign="top">I see that you are a new member here on DPChallenge.  Don''t let your placing in this, your first, challenge deter you from continuing if you are serious.   Participate in more challenges and in the forums.  There is a lot to learn from others on this site.</td>', 'I see that you are a new member here on DPChallenge.  Don''t let your placing in this, your first, challenge deter you from continuing if you are serious.   Participate in more challenges and in the forums.  There is a lot to learn from others on this site.', '2006-06-26 18:02:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2555638, 348171, 40718, '<td valign="top">Ya, that title is a tough one.  But more importantly, the shadows are placed just wrong.  I like them as part of the composition, but they fall across the man''s torso and head in just the right way that it isn''t obvious there is a person under there.  The confusion to the eye makes for a less appealing picture.  If this was posed, I would have reposed, if it wasn''t, well, then you are screwed.<br/> <br/>Nice composition otherwise.  Nice focus, nice B&amp;W conversion.</td>', 'Ya, that title is a tough one.  But more importantly, the shadows are placed just wrong.  I like them as part of the composition, but they fall across the man''s torso and head in just the right way that it isn''t obvious there is a person under there.  The confusion to the eye makes for a less appealing picture.  If this was posed, I would have reposed, if it wasn''t, well, then you are screwed. Nice composition otherwise.  Nice focus, nice B&W conversion.', '2006-06-26 18:10:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2555652, 348864, 40718, '<td valign="top">ya, another entrant learns the risk taken in entering the American flag.  I''m sure at least a few of the 1-3 scores were purely for that reason.<br/> <br/>That being said, you took a number of other risks as well.  Film grain.  Centered composition.  Selective desat.  Abstract interpretation of the challenge.  Basically this shot was a DPC minefield.  And you STILL scored a 5.51.  So I''d take the 5.5 as a man who walks away after being thrown 50 feet after crashing his motorcycle...</td>', 'ya, another entrant learns the risk taken in entering the American flag.  I''m sure at least a few of the 1-3 scores were purely for that reason. That being said, you took a number of other risks as well.  Film grain.  Centered composition.  Selective desat.  Abstract interpretation of the challenge.  Basically this shot was a DPC minefield.  And you STILL scored a 5.51.  So I''d take the 5.5 as a man who walks away after being thrown 50 feet after crashing his motorcycle...', '2006-06-26 18:15:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2555662, 348303, 40718, '<td valign="top">I''ll only briefly comment as I know you know what you are doing and a 5.8 isn''t a bad score.  BTW, take a look at my image grain entry.  Great minds must think alike.<br/> <br/>The first beef, and it''s small, is that I have no idea what he''s holding in his hand.  It''s even worse because it''s smack dab in the center of the picture and we puzzle over the object more than we take in the desolation of the picture.<br/> <br/>I also don''t quite like the way the word doesn''t make sense.  "apham"?  We also puzzle about what name ends with "apham".<br/> <br/>Those are small though.  Just off the top of my head.</td>', 'I''ll only briefly comment as I know you know what you are doing and a 5.8 isn''t a bad score.  BTW, take a look at my image grain entry.  Great minds must think alike. The first beef, and it''s small, is that I have no idea what he''s holding in his hand.  It''s even worse because it''s smack dab in the center of the picture and we puzzle over the object more than we take in the desolation of the picture. I also don''t quite like the way the word doesn''t make sense.  "apham"?  We also puzzle about what name ends with "apham". Those are small though.  Just off the top of my head.', '2006-06-26 18:20:47.000000', NULL, 0),
