(2556740, 349168, 14386, '<td valign="top">Hi David.  You''re on a roll.  Proud to be Pinoy.  I am here in Manila.  Wish I can shoot with you.</td>', 'Hi David.  You''re on a roll.  Proud to be Pinoy.  I am here in Manila.  Wish I can shoot with you.', '2006-06-27 01:11:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2556742, 349499, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i>I see you felt this added to the desolation feel, but I''d push you a bit and ask you how? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Metaphorically. It represents the sense of being overwhelmed by your environment, of losing your sense of identity. It even suggests death, the way the body is reclaimed by the earth. Yes, I''m a poet. :)<br/> <br/>But I also have a taste for the flatness of an image. I like the way this picture has one texture throughout and the dog as such is seen only as a disruption of the texture. Instead of "popping" from the frame, the dog humbly melds into the environment, and that humility is echoed in her expression.<br/> <br/>After all, I could have easily distinguished the dog from its environment by leaving in the color. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by DrAchoo:I see you felt this added to the desolation feel, but I''d push you a bit and ask you how?   Metaphorically. It represents the sense of being overwhelmed by your environment, of losing your sense of identity. It even suggests death, the way the body is reclaimed by the earth. Yes, I''m a poet. :) But I also have a taste for the flatness of an image. I like the way this picture has one texture throughout and the dog as such is seen only as a disruption of the texture. Instead of "popping" from the frame, the dog humbly melds into the environment, and that humility is echoed in her expression. After all, I could have easily distinguished the dog from its environment by leaving in the color. :)', '2006-06-27 01:12:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2556822, 349052, 42957, '<td valign="top">Good job, Annah! A worthy tribute.<br/> <br/>And yay, I went there!<br/> <br/>:)</td>', 'Good job, Annah! A worthy tribute. And yay, I went there! :)', '2006-06-27 01:33:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2556894, 349024, 5885, '<td valign="top">Looks like yiu have a bit of motion blur or camera shake here. The idea was strong for this challenge, but overall the processing or lack of it hurt your score.<br/> <br/>I think a really tight crop of the face would have made the photo a lot stronger.<br/> <br/>Glad to hear she''s doing fine. Cute as she can be.</td>', 'Looks like yiu have a bit of motion blur or camera shake here. The idea was strong for this challenge, but overall the processing or lack of it hurt your score. I think a really tight crop of the face would have made the photo a lot stronger. Glad to hear she''s doing fine. Cute as she can be.', '2006-06-27 01:53:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2557073, 349052, 35274, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sanx:</b></div><hr/><i> Good job, Annah! A worthy tribute.<br/> <br/>And yay, I went there!<br/> <br/>:) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Awsome! :-D</td>', 'Originally posted by sanx: Good job, Annah! A worthy tribute. And yay, I went there! :)   Awsome! :-D', '2006-06-27 02:55:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2557094, 348839, 42013, '<td valign="top">Now that i see the kid, the pic is really funny.  I guess he really is "out on a limb".  Sorry i missed it the first time.</td>', 'Now that i see the kid, the pic is really funny.  I guess he really is "out on a limb".  Sorry i missed it the first time.', '2006-06-27 03:01:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2557107, 348991, 42013, '<td valign="top">Not as high of a finisher as i expected.  I really liked the emptyness of this picture.  I love mountains of any type!  I dont think the moon was integral to the picture, especially as it related to the challenge.  Even though the pic uses negative space well, the feeling of desolation might have been strengthened with a little more of the barren mountain showing.  Loved the title and gave it a 7 FWIW.</td>', 'Not as high of a finisher as i expected.  I really liked the emptyness of this picture.  I love mountains of any type!  I dont think the moon was integral to the picture, especially as it related to the challenge.  Even though the pic uses negative space well, the feeling of desolation might have been strengthened with a little more of the barren mountain showing.  Loved the title and gave it a 7 FWIW.', '2006-06-27 03:04:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2557116, 349480, 53964, '<td valign="top">I posterised because I know very little PS and just couldn''t get it depressing enough any other way I tried :( <br/> <br/>I did try it with the tree both in and out, couldn''t decide, but I liked the big raindrop splashed in front of the tree, so decided to leave it.  I just wasn''t thrilled with the image overall, but didn''t know how to get it how I wanted, and couldn''t bear not to have that update button!<br/> <br/>Thanks all, for the comments :D</td>', 'I posterised because I know very little PS and just couldn''t get it depressing enough any other way I tried :(  I did try it with the tree both in and out, couldn''t decide, but I liked the big raindrop splashed in front of the tree, so decided to leave it.  I just wasn''t thrilled with the image overall, but didn''t know how to get it how I wanted, and couldn''t bear not to have that update button! Thanks all, for the comments :D', '2006-06-27 03:07:18.000000', NULL, 0),
